### ===================================================================
### Indoor Wi-Fi Heatmap Backend - Sample HTTP Requests
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client, Thunder Client, Postman, etc.
### ===================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Health Check & API Overview
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. POST /createBlock
### Creates a new block with lat, lon, block name, and floor map image
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/createBlock
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="blockName"

Floor 1 - Main Wing
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lat"

37.774929
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lon"

-122.419416
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="blockImage"; filename="floor_map.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./tests/sample_floor_plan.png
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. POST /calibrateBlock (Floor Plan Scale Calibration)
### Sets reference distance: 200px on image = 10 meters in real life
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/calibrateBlock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blockName": "Floor 1 - Main Wing",
  "pointA": { "x": 100, "y": 150 },
  "pointB": { "x": 300, "y": 150 },
  "realDistanceMeters": 10
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. POST /calculateDistance (Real-World Distance Between Any Two Points)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/calculateDistance
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blockName": "Floor 1 - Main Wing",
  "pointA": { "x": 100, "y": 150 },
  "pointB": { "x": 500, "y": 150 }
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. POST /addWifi
### Adds a Wi-Fi network configuration to an existing block
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/addWifi
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blockName": "Floor 1 - Main Wing",
  "ssid": "Office_5G",
  "band": "5GHz",
  "width": "80MHz",
  "security": "WPA2-PSK"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. POST /SSID/block
### Records user manual coordinate measurement with signal strength (dBm)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/SSID/block
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ssid": "Office_5G",
  "blockName": "Floor 1 - Main Wing",
  "location": {
    "lat": 37.774929,
    "lon": -122.419416
  },
  "coordinates": {
    "x": 3,
    "y": 4
  },
  "strength": -58,
  "band": "5GHz",
  "security": "WPA2-PSK",
  "estDistance": 4.2
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. POST /SSID/block (Additional Measurement Point)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/SSID/block
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ssid": "Office_5G",
  "blockName": "Floor 1 - Main Wing",
  "coordinates": {
    "x": 7,
    "y": 2
  },
  "strength": -72,
  "band": "5GHz",
  "security": "WPA2-PSK",
  "estDistance": 9.5
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. GET /SSID/block (Without cached image -> sends Base64 floor image)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/SSID/block?ssid=Office_5G&blockName=Floor%201%20-%20Main%20Wing&hasImage=false
Accept: application/json

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. GET /SSID/block (With cached image -> omits Base64 image)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/SSID/block?ssid=Office_5G&blockName=Floor%201%20-%20Main%20Wing&hasImage=true
Accept: application/json

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. GET /Office_5G/block (Dynamic Route Param Variant)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/Office_5G/block?blockName=Floor%201%20-%20Main%20Wing
Accept: application/json

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. GET /blocks (List all blocks or search nearby)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/blocks
Accept: application/json

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. POST /delete
### Deletes the block, its Wi-Fis, and removes the local image file
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blockName": "Floor 1 - Main Wing",
  "lat": 37.774929,
  "lon": -122.419416
}